{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And in all that.</b> Now he [Moses] mentioned the singular [form]; the sense is, all that I have said, they are my commandments and my ordinances — but not so the ordinances of other elohim. And he said, <b>You shall not invoke.</b> That you not invoke their names to swear by them, and also that their worshippers not be made to swear by them. And this is \"and it shall not be heard on your lips\" — that you make others swear by it, that you not say to the singular [form], \"Swear to me by your elohim\"."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:38.076328782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}